/**
* @mainpage RAMC: Remote Access Memory Channels
*
* Yadda Yadda Yadda
* 
* @section Introduction
* Remote Access Memory Channels (RAMC) is an experimental library to explore 
* RMA applications through a simple unidirectional RMA channel building block.
* The primary innovations are (i) 
* not following a monolithic synchronized window creation wherein every participating 
* process exposes a target window; (ii) lazy (or pairwise) synchronization that avoids 
* synchonizing fences; (iii) a version of RMA with notification that avoids 
* traditional explicit notification by leveraging Slingshot NIC hardware counters.
*
* @section Installation
* Currently RAMC only works on HPE Cray Slingshot systems, as it relies on 
* Slingshot-specific capabilities.
*
* @section ToDo
*
